From: Vahiru <nekovahiru@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] audio: aidl: primary: pace capture transfers by ALSA data availability

StreamPrimary::transfer() paced capture transfers with the synthetic wall-clock
sleep originally written for the emulator stub. Because MonoPipe reads are
non-blocking, the first two transfers after stream start observed an incomplete
burst and returned zero-filled silence (~170 ms), permanently offsetting live
audio by two blocks for the lifetime of the stream.

Wait for a full capture burst to arrive in the MonoPipe (up to 500 ms on the
first block after start and 3 block periods thereafter) before reading, falling
back to wall-clock silence padding only if the hardware stalls. Also fix
inputIoThread's partial-write retry loop to advance the source pointer by the
frames already written.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
